# Forms & Styling Patterns

## Form Implementation with createForm
```tsx
const { forwardFormContext, TextInput, SelectInput, DatePicker, TextArea } = createForm({
  zodSchema: entityFormSchema,
});

const EntityModal = forwardFormContext(
  ({ onClose, onSubmit, isLoading, initialValues }, ctx) => {
    return (
      <Modal onClose={onClose} title="Add Entity">
        <form onSubmit={ctx.handleSubmit(onSubmit)}>
          <Stack>
            <TextInput
              name="name"
              label="Entity Name"
              placeholder="Enter name"
            />
            <SelectInput
              name="status"
              label="Status"
              placeholder="Select status"
              options={[
                { label: "Active", value: "ACTIVE" },
                { label: "Inactive", value: "INACTIVE" },
              ]}
            />
            <DatePicker
              name="start_date"
              label="Start Date"
            />
            <TextArea
              name="description"
              label="Description"
              placeholder="Enter description"
            />
          </Stack>
          
          <Stack horizontal gap={12} justify="end" className="mt-mds-24">
            <Button intent="default" onClick={onClose}>
              Cancel
            </Button>
            <Button type="submit" intent="primary" loading={isLoading}>
              Save
            </Button>
          </Stack>
        </form>
      </Modal>
    );
  }
);
```

## Form Components
- `TextInput`: Basic text input with label and validation
- `SelectInput`: Dropdown with options array
- `DatePicker`: Date selection with proper formatting
- `TextArea`: Multi-line text input
- `RadioGroup`: Radio button groups for exclusive selection
- `CheckBoxGroup`: Checkbox groups for multiple selection
- `Switch`: Toggle switch for boolean values

## Styling Guidelines
- Use Tailwind utility classes; avoid arbitrary values
- Read-only fields get `bg-gray-50` styling
- Modal action buttons right-aligned in `Stack horizontal`
- Primary buttons use `intent="primary"`
- Destructive actions use `intent="danger"`
- Form spacing with `Stack` component and `gap` props

## Button Patterns
```tsx
// Primary action
<Button intent="primary" loading={isLoading}>
  Save Changes
</Button>

// Secondary action
<Button intent="default" onClick={onCancel}>
  Cancel
</Button>

// Destructive action
<Button intent="danger" onClick={onDelete}>
  Delete
</Button>
```

## Layout Patterns
- Use `Stack` for vertical layouts with consistent spacing
- Use `Stack horizontal` for horizontal button groups
- Use `justify="end"` for right-aligned actions
- Use `gap={12}` for consistent spacing between elements

